      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1902-05-30_WidnesExaminer_art0074" n="art0074">
        <head>Formation of a Lodge at Runcorn.</head>
        <p>Formation of a Lodge at Runcorn.</p>
        <p>On Saturday lhe Independent Order of Good lemplars was introduced into Runcorn by a public tea, open air meeting,and entertainment in the Ashridge-street Primi- tive Methodist 'mission room. A good musterof members from Dallastown, Leigh, Liverpool, St Helens, Widnes, and Runcorn sat down to tea. After this an open air meeting was held near the post office. Bro A Francis, IpDSJ T, took charge of the mceting,and was supported by Bra Rey J A:Lee, PG C. Sr. GB Walker, PG AS, ' Bra G Clarke, F D ES, Sister Woods, C and SJ T, and I others, in their tr,ght regalia. The chairman exp,ained that the object ot the meeting was to enlist the help and sympathy of all earnest total abstainers in the fight against tbe drink traffic in the formation of a Lodge of Template in Runcorn to get held of met' and women to maize them better citizns,and to teach them their duties and privileges. and so help to throttle the drink traffic befere the traffic throttled the country. Bro Rev J A Leo gave a very earoest and powerful address in which be appealed for pledges, workers and re-enlistment of old Good Templar. He hop d all in Itunzcrn would re-join the new Lodge that was to be formed that night in the Ashridgr-strect mission room at the foot of the bridge. Bra J Warburton recited "While' the Sabbath bells are ringing Mr P J Illld, missioner, also gave an earnest appeal, and inetarCed several cases of poverty through drink' An adjournment was then made to the Mission Room. where an entertainment was given, presided over a Bee A W Eyre, who gave a cordial welcome to the good template, and ureed others to become total abstainers. He should be very glad to help the cause in Runcorn. Sengs were rendered by Sister Mrs Williams and Bra T Anders, and a recitation by Sister Mrs Francis.—Bro G B Walker gave an address upon Good Ternplary, and stated that during last year there had been established a new branch fer every day in the year, while 1,300 new members had been added. Bra Rev J A Lee gave an address, and again urged the claims of good temnlary. after which a hew lodge was formedsand named the "Runcorn Forwards."—Bro A Francis was the Instituting officer, and 13 members were admitted. Several are ready to be admitted at the nest meeting on Atnnday nrxt.—lt was decided to meet every Monday t 7.30 in the Abbridve-crr,,et 7.lisnion Room.</p>
        <p>Local Soldier 111 of Enteric. Frain Wednesday eight's casualf-r list, ißcued by the War Office, it appears that 4,407 John Naughton, Ist South Lancashire Regiment, was al of enteric at Lady— smith on May 26th.</p>
        <p>PEOPLE WILL TALK RFOLII the goad Pa4lo they get he ALP. TAYLOR'S GOOD BOOM—Advt.</p>
